Subject: [PATCH] [M156] Guard against transfer buffer ID wraparound

Original change's description:
> Guard against transfer buffer ID wraparound
>
> If the positive int32 space is exhausted just crash. There should never
> be enough transfer buffer allocations to exhaust the ID space so this is
> a defensive guard against intentionally exhausting the ID space to cause
> wrap around. Wraparound could cause ID confusion and potential give a
> site access to resources for a different site hosted in the same
> renderer process.
>
